{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgZAWHoNKbqvFU9K23AdP","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01LuebC6TJUSgJHtR6Xhm7NY","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /data/summereunann/neurico-workspaces/temperature_calibration_gaps_20261030_120000_ab12cd34; python3 - <<'EOF'\np='REPORT.md'; s=open(p).read()\nfor a,b in [\n(\"pass@4 exceeds greedy by up to 16.5 points (Qwen2.5-1.5B),\\n  and by 6–15 points for the other models.\",\"pass@4 exceeds greedy pass@1 by 6–18 points in every\\n  model, with the largest gain on Qwen2.5-3B (+18.3).\"),\n(\"(changes range from −5.0 to +1.6 points)\",\"(changes range from −5.0 to +1.7 points)\"),\n(\"by 4–8× the seed noise floor\",\"by 4–7× the seed noise floor\"),\n(\"`sem_div` increases at every T until too few coherent groups remain\",\"`sem_div` increases at almost every T until too few coherent groups remain\"),\n(\"The p-values above are from 10,000 sign-flip permutations, so \\\"<.001\\\" is the resolution limit.\",\"P-values come from 10,000 sign-flip permutations, so \\\"<.001\\\" is near the resolution limit. Holm correction here and\\nin 5.3 was applied over all 12 runs, including the two controls.\"),\n]:\n    assert a in s,a; s=s.replace(a,b)\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\ncat > README.md <<'EOF'\n# Temperature Calibration Gaps\n\nHow softmax temperature (0–2.0) affects diversity and quality across 10 open-weight models on stories (WritingPrompts),\nfactual QA (TriviaQA) and code (HumanEval). All models ran locally because no API key was available, so hosted frontier\nmodels were not tested.\n\n## Key findings\n- **Quality drops off a cliff, and the location depends on the model.** Story T_u (coherence ≥90% of peak) runs from\n  0.84 for Qwen2.5-0.5B to 1.31 for Qwen2.5-14B.\n- **Open-ended:** diversity stops improving, but much of the apparent plateau is measurement (metric ceiling, word\n  salad embedding alike). Coherence loss usually exceeds the predicted 20–40%: 48–63% at T = 1.4 in 9/10 models.\n- **Factual QA:** T = 0.8–1.0 is worse than T ≤ 0.7 in 9/10 models, but by only 0.7–5.2 points, and coverage@4 gains\n  nothing further above 0.7.\n- **Code:** the \"useful range 0.2–0.6, collapse above 0.8\" claim is refuted. No model drops significantly from 0.6 to\n  0.8, and five models peak at greedy. Qwen ≥3B and Gemma stay near peak to T ≈ 1.1–1.4.\n- **Size and family:** larger Qwen models tolerate higher T on all tasks, but Llama only on QA. Llama's story cliff stays\n  at T ≈ 1.0 from 1B to 8B. Family differences at matched size are 4–7× the seed noise floor.\n\nFull details, caveats and tables are in [REPORT.md](REPORT.md).\n\n## Reproduce\n```bash\nUV_CACHE_DIR=$PWD/.uv_cache uv sync\n./run_all.sh     # needs a GPU, local HF cache, and a Qwen3-8B OpenAI-compatible server on :8011\n```\nRe-run the analysis only: `NUMPY_MADVISE_HUGEPAGE=0 .venv/bin/python src/analyze.py`\n\n## Files\n- `planning.md`: motivation and pre-experiment plan\n- `src/`: `prep_data.py`, `worker.py` (generation), `score.py`, `judge.py`, `analyze.py`, `error_analysis.py`\n- `results/gens/`: raw outputs; `results/scores/`, `results/judge/`: metrics; `results/analysis/`: tables\n- `results/judge_audit.md`: manual check of the judge\n- `figures/`: plots used in the report\nEOF\nuntil ! pgrep -u $USER -f \"src/[a]nalyze.py\" >/dev/null; do sleep 5; done; tail -n 1 logs/analyze_rerun.log | cut -c1-100; for f in curves:curves_run1 h3_code:h3_run1 h5_family:h5_run1; do cmp results/analysis/${f%%:*}.csv /tmp/${f##*:}.csv && echo \"${f%%:*} identical\"; done; ls REPORT.md README.md planning.md figures/*.png; pgrep -u $USER -f \"[w]orker.py|[p]ost_pipeline|[g]pu_holder\" -a | cut -c1-100; nvidia-smi --query-compute-apps=pid,used_memory --format=csv,noheader | head; true","description":"Fix report figures, write README, verify rerun","timeout":590000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_d