{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgZC4H9g9acnvaZSYJKvj","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The research is finished: all 12 runs completed (10 models plus 2 controls, about 277,000 samples), and `REPORT.md` and `README.md` contain the actual results. Quality doesn't decline gradually with temperature. It stays nearly flat, then falls sharply at a point that varies by model, so the hypothesis's fixed thresholds don't fit any single model well.\n\n| Hypothesis clause | Verdict | What happened |\n|---|---|---|\n| Open-ended: diversity plateaus above 1.2, coherence drops 20–40% | Partly supported | Diversity stops improving, peaking at T = 1.0–1.4 in 9 of 10 models, but much of that is a measurement effect. Coherence usually falls more than predicted: 48–63% at T = 1.4 in 9 of 10 models. |\n| Factual QA: above 0.7, accuracy degrades with no meaningful diversity gain | Mostly supported, small effect | T = 0.8–1.0 is significantly worse than T ≤ 0.7 in 9 of 10 models, but only by 0.7–5.2 points. Chance that any of 4 samples is right stops improving above 0.7. |\n| Code: useful range 0.2–0.6, sharp collapse above 0.8 | Refuted as stated | No model drops significantly from 0.6 to 0.8, and greedy (T = 0) is best for 5 of 10 models. Qwen models of 3B and up, plus Gemma, stay near peak to T ≈ 1.1–1.4. |\n| Smaller models have narrower useful ranges | Supported for Qwen, weak for Llama | Qwen shows it on all three tasks, though only barely for code. Llama shows it only on QA, and its story coherence breaks at T ≈ 1.0 from 1B through 8B. |\n| Curve shape differs across families at the same scale | Supported | Llama differs from the other families by 4–7× the seed noise. Qwen and Mistral are close to each other. |\n\n**Limits on these results:**\n- **Models:** no API key was available, so all models ran locally. GPT, Claude and Gemini were not tested.\n- **Literature:** `literature_review.md`, `papers/` and `code/` were never created. The papers I cite are from memory and unverified, and the report says so.\n- **Precision:** models of 3B and up used quantized AWQ weights, so precision varies with size. A bf16 control showed curve shapes are unaffected, but absolute scores are lower: greedy code pass@1 was .768 vs .829.\n- **Coherence judge:** it rarely scores below 3, even on gibberish, and agreed with my own labels on only 12 of 16 borderline stories. Some analysis choices, including the use of the coherent rate (judge score ≥ 5) for story useful ranges, were made after seeing partial data, and the report lists them.\n- **Family vs checkpoint:** each family and size has only one checkpoint, so the two can't be separated. Mistral's low code score (.27) is unexplained; it isn't caused by the missing-imports scoring issue I tested.\n\n**Reproducibility:** re-running the analysis gave byte-identical output for the three tables I compared (curves, code, family). Generation was not re-run in full; only Qwen2.5-0.5B has a second-seed run, and it showed no significant differences.\n\nMy GPU workers are stopped, and I added this session's host lessons to memory. Nothing is committed. Git in this directory reports a dubious-ownership error for `/data`, so that needs sorting out before committing.\n\nStart with `REPORT.md`; the raw outputs and tables are under `results/`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":523,"cache_read_input_tokens":300254,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":523},"output_tokens":792,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2332c03a-08c0-4a8b-a3ed-e94c26a471d1","uuid":"62ffc530-5940-4faa-bb70-96037e7eb063","timestamp":"2026-10-30T22:14:03.954Z","request_id":"req_011CgZC4Gx2YwxV2iRsN4Jj6"}
